As a Self-Service Developer, I would like to add new Page of the API Onboarding flow, named Resources, so that users can add their external resource links outside of AMC during the API Onboarding process.

Context: 

As part of API Catalog Requirements, Supporting Documentation Linkage will cover these requirements, REQ-55, REQ-114, REQ-119, REQ-121.

We want to give users a centralized place within API Details to link all specific external and internal resources related to the API. This includes official chalk documentation, github repos, test documentation, diagrams, and troubleshooting links. Doing so, we need to add this page during the API Onboarding process for users to populate those fields.

Implementation Details:

See mocks for look and feel details:

Incorporate this in all Flows (Net new, Update, Admin Review, and Add Version Flows)
Add an additional Page on the API Onboarding Form. Make Plugins page to be Page 3, and Make new Resources as page 4 at the top navigation bar.
Label the top of the page as "Supporting Resources" in charter blue color.
Add a helpful tool note stating "Note: Adding Architecture, Design, Glossary, Source Repo, and Test Result links helps reviewers and consumers quickly understand, and confidently user your API. "{}
Category Dropdown.

Category dropdown list will consist of 4 selections. "Official Chalk Documentation*, Source Control*, API References, and Testing References".

The list of categories is fetched from the backend via GET API call when the page is loaded.
GET pinxt-selfservice/v1/api-resources/categories
Ensure that the Official Chalk Documentation and Source Control have a red asterisk at the end of the text, meaning this is mandatory category.
Ensure every Category section is populated in a line from top to bottom.
Ensure all the dropdowns are greyed out and italicized and disabled.
Sub-Categories

Official Chalk Documentation Selection

If user selects this selection, automatically prepopulate the sub-categories and Resource links dynamically.
We are still allowing users to select the dropdown even though we are populating the sub categories for them in the section. But disable the selections for the dropdown. Grey and italicize them. 
First dropdown field is "Design/Overview/General
Second dropdown field is "Architecture". 
Third dropdown field is "Sequence Diagram"
If the user selects any of these sub categories once - ensure that the required link is shown in red and the message below is populated.
The other remainder subcategories are optional.
Ensure that at least ONE required resource link sub category is populated correctly. The other Optional ones can be empty.
These dropdowns will be fetched dynamically from backend GET call when the selection is selected.
GET pinxt-selfservice/v1/api-resources/categories
Source Control Selection

If user selects this selection, automatically prepopulate the sub-categories and Resource links dynamically. We are still allowing users to select the dropdown even though we are populating the sub categories for them in the section. But disable the selections for the dropdown. Grey and italicize them. 
First dropdown field is "Primary*".
For this sub-category, also spawn a required line item named Resource Link* in red with a small tooltip beneath stating "Resource Link is required."
For source control section, allow the user to select the in section plus button to spawn a new dropdown line item and display Primary as greyed out and italicized, but display Config and Infrastructure as selectable options.
Once selected, the desired selection and resource link will appear as Optional Fields. Do not include the required red and the required help tool for Optional Sub-Categories.
API References and Testing References Selection

If user selects these selection, automatically prepopulate the sub-categories and Resource links dynamically.
Since these Categories and sub-categories are Optional, ensure that no required options are given.
User is still only able to select 1 sub category at one time.
Ensure the Resource Links are spawning after the Sub-Category is selected.
Resource Links Validations:

Refer to our previous implementations on URL standards: https://chalk.charter.com/spaces/PINXTSS/pages/3100872351/URL+Standards
If the given value doesn't meet URL standards, show and an error "Invalid URL, please enter a valid URL."
Empty field: If user has a required Resource link empty but tries to proceed to next page without entering URL, spawn error message under URL "Required Resource Links cannot be empty. Please enter a valid link."
Navigation

Ensure the same navigation buttons of Cancel, Next, and Reset Form are displayed at the bottom like the other pages.
Ensure that the user cannot navigate to the next page until all required categories and subcategories with all valid Resource Links are inputted.
Spawn Error message under the Next and Cancel button if there are open Required fields/invalid Resource Links needing their attention in red. "Please complete all required categories and/or enter valid resource links to proceed to next page."
 

Logic Scenarios:

Default: Description, unless required subcategories, then spawn the required subcategory.
Upon Swagger change/Swagger upload: unaffected with swagger changes
Navigating b/w pages: unaffected. Retain user's input.
Navigating away from API Onboarding: Reset
Modifications directly in Supporting Resource Section: are final. 
User Role specific restrictions - None
Flow related restrictions ( New Onboarding, Update, Review, Simple Edit, Add Version) - None
 

Acceptance Criteria:

Page 4 is now Supporting Resource Page, and Page 3 is Plugins, Page 5 is API summary page.
This section should be available in all flows. Look and feel should match mock screens.
Required Categories and Sub-Categories are required upon proceeding to next page.
User is only able to select 1 category at one time, no multi select. Hide Section "+" once all 4 section and the all 4 categories are added.
The app should validate that url starts with https://, only 1 link per URL Field, no empty fields per sub-category selected.
Ensure that the Dropdown and Categories that are Optional, are optional.
When Editing/Re-Submitting, previously saved value should be pre-selected automatically.
When API Onboarding form is submitted, the backend call(s) should reflect the same value as of what user have selected for monitoring links.
POST https://apis-internal-corp.shared.dev-spectrum.net/pinxt-selfservice/v1/dashboard
PATCH https://apis-internal-corp.shared.dev-spectrum.net/pinxt-selfservice/v1/dashboard/{requestId} 
 
POST https://apis-internal-corp.shared.dev-spectrum.net/pinxt-selfservice/v1/apis
PATCH https://apis-internal-corp.shared.dev-spectrum.net/pinxt-selfservice/v1/apis/{apiId}
Add new unit tests to prove the correctness of this enhancement
Regression should continue to pass.
Test Team to add Test Results & Screenshots at the time of Closing the story. 
In all the flows, the manager/developer/admin should be able to change this monitoring value. 
Test Curls are to be attached.
UI Shouldn't Break
